# Credentials never enter an image, and neither does anything the build does not read.
# "If this file exists, the files and directories that match patterns in the files are removed from
# the build context before it's sent to the builder" (Docker, Build context): a file listed here is
# never sent, so a key or a sibling checkout can neither reach a layer nor fail the build unreadable.
# TDD-identity-control-001 §The Migrate Image and Its Exceptions.
.env
**/.env
.git
.github
coverage
cov-src
*.out
.atlas

# Private keys and key rings: deploy/dev/keys/ and any other keys/ directory, and a stray *.pem.
**/keys/
*.pem
**/*.pem

# The sibling repositories deploy-dev checks out into this workspace (identity-kernel as .kernel,
# identity-experience as .experience), and the image scan's working directory. None is built here,
# and the kernel's checkout holds its signing keystore readable by its owner alone.
.kernel/
.experience/
.image-scan/
